  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The advertisement, by virtue of its siting on the public highway, would cause harm to the visual amenity of the streetscene in an area which is already constrained in terms of the presence of other street furniture and infrastructure. Additionally the development would reduce the footway available to pedestrians, thereby causing harm to pedestrian movements and users of the public highway, where the full width of the footway is considered necessary for pedestrians. Considering these cumulative impacts, the proposal would cause harm to visual amenity, would be a hazard to public safety and therefore fails to comply with Policies 53 and 59 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
